  "notes": "An auxiliary verb that attaches to verb stems to express continuing an action without stopping.\n\nPATTERN:\nVerb masu-stem + {続|つづ}ける\n- {食|た}べ + {続|つづ}ける = {食|た}べ{続|つづ}ける (keep eating)\n- {走|はし}り + {続|つづ}ける = {走|はし}り{続|つづ}ける (keep running)\n- {働|はたら}き + {続|つづ}ける = {働|はたら}き{続|つづ}ける (keep working)\n\nCONJUGATION:\nConjugates as an ichidan verb: {続|つづ}けない, {続|つづ}けます, {続|つづ}けて, {続|つづ}けた\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\nEmphasizes persistence and duration. Often implies effort or determination: {諦|あきら}めずに{挑戦|ちょうせん}し{続|つづ}ける (keep trying without giving up).\n\nSIMILAR GRAMMAR:\n- 〜ている: ongoing state (neutral)\n- 〜{始|はじ}める: to begin doing\n- 〜{終|お}わる: to finish doing",
